WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:08.800
… I request you,
because the people that read the magazine,

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:13.360
they are much more
interested in the person, in a way,

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:18.880
and also in what you think
about the daily life.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:19.840
Oh, yes, very important.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.840
Because, what I am trying to do…

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.680
This is very dynamic for daily life.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:27.600
It must be. It must be practical.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:32.960
To, integrate the spiritual…

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.560
It is integrated already.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:35.600
You know, into the…

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.040
I understand, I understand.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:40.320
It’s absolutely integrated already.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:44.400
Because here in Germa-in the West,
usually you make, you…

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:45.600
Separately.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:46.160
Separated.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:47.040
That’s wrong.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:51.120
They sit in the next room
and outside they make big wars.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:59.200
Yes. That’s true. That is disintegration.
That’s true.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:07.760
Is it okay? You’ve got power?

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:18.720
Yes, I think so. Ha, ha, ha. Yes, fine.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.440
Yes, my first question would be,
why are there hardly any female

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:32.560
gurus ever been and also today?

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:37.600
Not in India. We had, in ancient times,
many women who were regarded

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:48.800
as great orators, great poets, as saints,
you see. Many are there. In recent years,

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:53.200
also we can say, about four hundred,
five hundred years back,

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:56.000
we had great saints as ladies in India.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.640
We don’t have this
discrimination in India,

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:02.560
this kind of a thing,
where a woman cannot be a saint or…

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:04.480
it’s available to everyone.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:09.920
On the contrary, in India the woman is
the power of the man. She is the power.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:12.720
Like when you have to say Rama’s name,
they’ll say Sita-Rama.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:16.160
So Sita comes first.
If they have to say Krishna’s name,

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:18.480
they say Radha-Krishna.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:20.640
Women are very much respected in India.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.880
And it’s said that,
“Where the women are respected

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:27.200
and they are respectable,
there reside the gods”.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:30.400
So India has a very different concept.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:33.200
But the gurus who came out in the market,
you see,

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:37.280
‘marketing spirit’ is that of men,
you see. They want to market everything.

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:40.880
So women didn’t have
that much sense of marketing, I think,

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:42.080
so they didn’t come out.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:46.400
But I think there are one
or two who did do this kind of a job of

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:49.280
marketing ‘gurudama’. Yes, they did it.

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:52.560
Yes,
so that’s why one talks about Guru Nanak

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:55.415
and all, but no, I don’t know…

00:02:55.415 --> 00:02:56.400
No, there are, there are.
One female name.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:59.840
We don’t call a woman by guru,
but we call them saints, you see.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:02.320
Like we have Janabai in India.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:10.560
We had another one, very famous one,
called Sakubai in India. So many. And

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:13.200
then Gyaneshwara’s sister was Muktabai.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.840
We had all of them.
They are called as saints, you see.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:22.640
We had many ladies. But only in this West,
you see, women are not ordained

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:25.360
and all that nonsense.
I can’t understand it.

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:28.800
Because in India women are regarded
to be more spiritual than men,

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:33.113
much more evolved than men. Yes,
that’s what we believe.

00:03:33.113 --> 00:03:36.560
But do you think they are much more maybe,
in the house, and not

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:41.505
so on the market in a more public sense,
or is it even in public?

00:03:41.505 --> 00:03:45.120
They could be, if it needs come to,
they are better than men.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:48.800
But if there is need,
like we had queens who fought the wars,

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:50.080
you see. But…

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:50.640
Queens?

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.920
Yes, Jhansi ki Rani, Ahilyabai Holkar.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:56.720
We had so many, Chand Bibi, so many women.

00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:01.360
But their assertion was
like a power behind the scene.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:04.480
But when it came to them,
they came out on the horses.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:09.520
We had great women in our country,
very great women, like Nur Jahan. Great,

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:13.760
great women and of great quality
and character.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:18.400
Our Prime Minister was also a woman,
like that.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.400
Yes, you’re talking about Miss Gandhi.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:24.320
Yes, Miss Gandhi was there.
She was a woman after all.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:32.400
And Gandhiji said that the first Prime
Minister should be a

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.160
scheduled caste woman.

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:42.160
Ah, yes. But would this…
do you think even these saints,

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:50.080
these women saints would be as highly
developed in their spiritual path as men?

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:51.200
Of course.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:52.080
Ah, yes.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:56.000
Of course, they are very much respected,
very much respected

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:02.080
and are regarded as very, the highest,
as for example, in India,

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:05.200
say more than Christ,
they worship the Mother of Christ,

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.440
in India.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:08.400
Oh, do they?

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.400
Yes, they do.

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:12.000
You’re talking about the Christians?

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:16.640
Yes, of course. Not only the Christians,
non-Christians also. If it’s a mother,

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:18.800
then it doesn’t matter
whether you are Muslim,

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:20.640
Hindu or Christian in India.

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:24.400
We have temples, we call them Mat Mawli,
means the mother.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:26.880
Then if she’s the mother,
she’s the mother everywhere.

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:32.960
And you’ll be surprised even
when this Portuguese came,

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:37.040
what was his name, the Portuguese
who came to India first time? Was,

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:41.520
went back in Portugal
and he told the king that,

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:46.000
“They are all Christians
because they are not like Muslims,

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.360
they worship the Mother.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:50.880
So they are Christians”. Vasco da Gama.

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:52.160
He was the first who came.

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:54.320
And he went and told the king like this.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:58.000
So that time also, you see,
even the Christians worshipped the Mother,

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.480
because he went and said,
“They cannot be Muslims,

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:03.600
they are absolutely Christians
because they worship the Mother”.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:04.160
Oh, yes.

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:07.440
Yes, because when he went to Goa,
he found there’s a very

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:12.000
beautiful temple of a goddess. So he said,
“They worship Mother as a goddess. So,

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:15.120
they cannot be Muslims”.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:16.880
Ah, yes, I understand.

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:21.120
And also, among Muslims like Shias,
they worship a goddess.

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:28.640
We should not say goddess but saint,
this Fatima, Khadija,

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:31.280
all of them are respected as saints.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:40.160
What, to your life, speaking of your life,
what kind of education did you have?

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:41.120
I had a, yeah….

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:42.800
You seem to be…

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:43.920
Very knowledgeable.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:47.920
Yes, perhaps to have some kind of
Western education in a way.

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:50.000
No, no, not at all, not at all.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:54.160
I just- you see, my education in English
has been very minimum, I should say,

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:57.040
because I was studying
in a vernacular language.

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:00.800
My father was a great patriot,
vernacular language. You see,

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:04.000
one of the Indian languages.
And medium of instruction

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:08.640
was a one of them,
Marathi as my mother tongue.

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:10.320
That’s what I studied in.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:13.040
And then we had only one little
book called ‘Great Expectation’,

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:17.120
a small thing.
I didn’t study English much because

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:21.360
then I joined science college,
and then I joined medical college so there

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:23.600
was no question of learning any language.

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:27.440
But somehow, I have an aptitude, I think,
for languages and everything.

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:30.000
And most of my knowledge
comes from within.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.588
I have not read about it.

00:07:31.588 --> 00:07:33.672
From within?
Yes, from within, yes.

00:07:33.672 --> 00:07:33.680
Ah, yes.

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:36.160
Because you are knowledge, after all,
if you become the knowledge,

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:37.200
you get all the knowledge.

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:38.400
From within.

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:39.280
Yes.

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:47.840
But because you just mentioned medical,
it was the traditional Indian medical…

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:50.880
No, no, no, no. I did medicine myself.
For two years,

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:53.280
I did medicine just to know how,
what they talk.

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:55.840
But I was not interested in
getting a degree or anything.

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:58.640
But I did study medicine to understand.

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:02.640
I also read some books.
I should have read more the

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:04.800
dictionary of psychology
to understand what the

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:07.520
psychologists are talking.
Because I knew what it was,

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:10.080
but I didn’t know what
human beings called it. So,

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:12.560
I had to know the terminology.

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:16.320
Ah, yes. But that is a kind of …

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:18.069
Rapport, for the rapport.

00:08:18.069 --> 00:08:18.080
Body and…

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:20.960
So that I could talk to doctors,
I could talk to psychiatrists,

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:23.760
I could see what their problems are.

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:33.360
Ah, yes. Because I’ve read a bit about the
Tibetan medical care and the Chinese,

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:35.600
and it’s very different to the Western.

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:38.640
So I thought maybe the Indian
is also very different,

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:39.680
the original Indian.

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:42.960
Yes, you see,
our style is called as Ayurveda in India.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:48.960
But that also starts with three doshas,
three defects in a human being.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:56.400
And they deal with it in those ways,
that there are three main troubles,

00:08:56.400 --> 00:08:58.720
which I’ll be talking today about that.

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:04.480
That is either a person is having a
left side or a right side or a central.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:08.240
So there are three types of people
and they have three types of troubles.

00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:10.080
So accordingly, they should be treated.

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:12.320
Because they start with the fundamental.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:16.960
So if the fundamentals are correct,
then it is easy to treat a patient

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:23.280
because we don’t create imbalances,
as we do not deal from outside.

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:26.880
Like you see a symptom outside,
a person now supposing,

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:29.440
you have a symptom,
say you get a blister on the hand

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:31.200
or something.
Then you start treating that,

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:33.840
but you don’t treat the
fundamental problem, you see.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:35.360
So it is the other way round.

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:39.840
But ours is even subtler than that,
because we treat the chakras.

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:44.065
Ah, yes. And then you married, you, you…

00:09:44.065 --> 00:09:46.720
Yes, very much.
You did the conventional Indian…

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:49.520
Of course, absolutely,
I’m a conventional Indian woman.

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:52.000
I’m married
and my husband is the Secretary

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:55.520
General of the International
Maritime Organization, in London. So…

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:57.120
That’s why you live in London.

00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:01.600
We are very much married
and I have grandchildren also,

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:02.480
four grandchildren.

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:04.954
And how many own children?

00:10:04.954 --> 00:10:05.440
I beg your pardon?
My own children?

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:06.480
My own, two daughters.

00:10:06.480 --> 00:10:07.120
two daughters.

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:09.920
The elder daughter is now
about forty years of age.

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:15.120
And don’t you regret not
to live in India anymore?

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:16.720
India, I go quite often.

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:18.720
Ah, yes.
You don’t stay in London all the time?

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:21.760
All the time, no.
I’m in India for about three months

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:24.400
and everywhere, I’m travelling everywhere.

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:27.280
I have an Indian passport.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:34.160
Yesterday, you said something,
I understood it that way…

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:35.840
Will you have some coffee, please?

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:38.143
Yes, a bit.

00:10:38.143 --> 00:10:39.808
Would you like a cup of coffee, Mother?

00:10:39.808 --> 00:10:40.800
I’ll have it, I’ll have it. Thank you.

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:42.720
You drink coffee?

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:44.240
Yes, anything I can…

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:48.560
Because I’ve heard, well,
coffee might be very heavy.

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:50.000
Nothing harms me much.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:50.480
No?

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:54.000
No. I even take Coca-Cola
because I have to be very normal, you see,

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.600
in the modern times. It’s all right.

00:10:56.400 --> 00:11:00.240
I could not tolerate Coca-Cola before,
because it had some funny things in it.

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:04.080
But now it’s all right.
Anything that is not intoxicant,

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:06.400
I can take.

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:12.640
You said yesterday something
that struck my ear.

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:15.760
You said the Germans should…

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:17.760
Save the world.

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:21.360
Save the world, yes!
What did you mean by that?

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:24.800
You see, because they’re so advanced,
otherwise, you see, in every way,

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:27.040
Germans are very much advanced.

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:34.144
In machinery, everything,
they are very systematic.

00:11:34.144 --> 00:11:34.160
But spiritually.

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:41.600
Yes, with rather too much of a,
what you say, it’s a very good…

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:46.000
As in machinery we have produced robots,
we have produced Germans, I would say,

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:50.240
that kind of thing. Now,
if a robot can become a spiritual thing,

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:52.960
then imagine what will
happen to the whole world!

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:56.160
You think that’s a very
good starting point.

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:58.960
Very good. They can…
once they become that,

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:03.840
then nothing like it. I mean,
they can destroy or they can save.

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:08.560
Because they’re very determined people.
Very determined.

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:11.760
If you fix up something into their heads,
then they will go ahead.

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:14.160
But that’s a difficult part.

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:16.560
Maybe that’s too much ego.

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:21.200
I must say it is.
Anything that is pampering their ego,

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:24.640
they would like.
But something where they have to

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:27.680
surrender their ego is rather difficult.

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:30.080
But once they start, you see,
seeing the knowledge,

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:35.520
that is there in the Divine,
then they just surrender to it.

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:40.080
Because they think it’s all non-knowledge.

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:46.560
I also think that Germans, somehow,
have a very strong connection to death,

00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:57.920
to everything that is also
connected to suffering and to tears, to…

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:04.960
to pain. Pain in a deeper,
in a soul sense.

00:13:06.080 --> 00:13:10.720
Would you think this has a
connection to their spiritual value?

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:14.160
I mean, they feel the pain of others,
you mean to say?

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:19.680
They feel the pain of the material world.

00:13:19.680 --> 00:13:20.560
You think so?

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:22.000
Yes, I think so.

00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:27.120
They react, you mean to say, of the…
They react, yes.

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:29.120
But in a very different way.

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:33.200
In a very different way, I would say,
like this now, ‘Bauhaus’ is,

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:40.800
let us take one thing like ‘Bauhaus’ is,
is that they thought that houses should be

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:46.960
simple and they should be not elaborate.

00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:50.960
They should not be…
the lines should not move much,

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:55.520
I mean to say. And there
where I think they make mistakes,

00:13:55.520 --> 00:14:01.680
that simplicity doesn’t mean
that it is no beauty. You see,

00:14:01.680 --> 00:14:05.600
beauty is very important for life,
is the essence of life.

00:14:05.600 --> 00:14:09.200
If you make everything simple,
it’s very boring, you know.

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:13.120
And a person can really become mad with
that kind of a thing.

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:16.720
So beauty is very important.
And that beauty can be

00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:22.880
made available to people,
if people are allowed to use

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:26.240
more hands than use machinery.

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:29.040
But you see,
the way people started off with this

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:32.320
industrial revolution
in the Western world,

00:14:32.320 --> 00:14:34.960
what happened that complete,
their hands have become just

00:14:34.960 --> 00:14:39.120
like machines now,
they can’t make anything of their own.

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:47.280
So now if they still encourage the living
with few things but beautiful things,

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:51.760
instead of having so much plastic
that you make a mountain out of that,

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:56.480
then you see, this kind of an idea
that they have of simplicity,

00:14:56.480 --> 00:14:58.320
I do not believe in that.

00:14:58.320 --> 00:15:01.520
Even in India if you go,
even if it’s a villager, he may be poor,

00:15:01.520 --> 00:15:07.440
he may be using cow dung to clean
his house and paint it with,

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:11.840
but he’ll make it beautiful patterns
and things, everywhere.

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:16.880
It’s not like Bauhaus.
Bauhaus is frightening to Me,

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:19.120
because all such houses
will make people mad.

00:15:19.120 --> 00:15:21.680
And they are doing now in America,
they feel,

00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:26.000
because the lines have not moved,
you’ll feel you are living in a hospital.

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:31.920
So simplicity should not be confused:
nature is simple but so beautiful.

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:36.800
Yes,
but maybe some people have the need to

00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:41.120
develop themselves further
after becoming mad. If you,

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:42.800
or let’s say it in a different way…

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:48.000
I follow your point quite all right, yes,
yes. That’s a wrong conception.

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:49.760
Absolute wrong conception.

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:52.000
If you become mad, you’ll become madder.

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:55.840
You can never, it’s like to make it clean,
you make it dirty. It’s like that.

00:15:55.840 --> 00:15:58.000
It’s a very wrong conception, upside down.

00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:04.000
But what about Kali?
Kali is a symbol as the dark woman,

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:08.880
as the dark goddess, that you go through
darkness to go to the light.

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:10.080
I mean, that’s a different thing.

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:14.240
Kali is a Goddess. Nothing can touch her.

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:18.080
Wherever she is, she can go to any point
and can cure people.

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:20.240
She can do what she likes. She is Kali.

00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:22.000
You are not. You are a human being.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:25.600
If you put your hand in the mud,
your hand will be soiled.

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:27.113
If you give it to a snake…

00:16:27.113 --> 00:16:29.440
Then I find my direction
to something else, maybe.

00:16:29.440 --> 00:16:32.240
No, no, no.
Your direction should be to become

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:35.360
like Kali, first of all. To ascend.

00:16:35.360 --> 00:16:38.000
So the first thing is to ascend.

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:44.000
Isn’t that descent?
Don’t I descend to Kali?

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:45.840
Yes, I mean, no, not descent.

00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:52.400
But if you try to just copy Kali,
you cannot do it. Just by, say,

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:55.840
supposing you crucify anyone,
he doesn’t become Christ.

00:16:55.840 --> 00:17:00.960
Speaking of the Germans again,
what do you think about the Third Reich?

00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:04.960
What do you think it meant,
as a collective happening,

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:06.480
what Germans were looking for?

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:11.747
Third eye is a… That’s a third eye,
again he got…

00:17:11.747 --> 00:17:15.720
Third Reich. It’s the Nazi time.

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:18.446
It’s the Nazi kingdom, Shri Mataji,
the Nazi ruled in Germany.

00:17:18.446 --> 00:17:20.240
Oh, whoa, whoa, that’s horrible!
What do you think of the Nazis?

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:24.000
Yes, because I’m asking you,
what do you think it meant for

00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:25.760
the German people as a collective?

00:17:25.760 --> 00:17:27.600
They should oppose it, absolutely.

00:17:27.600 --> 00:17:29.600
Outright, I mean. This is terrible.

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:32.160
Poor things, you see,
one political mistake of theirs,

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:36.240
now Germans are looked down
upon by everyone for one reason,

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:38.080
somebody made a mistake like that.

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:40.960
You see, he pampered your ego,
first of all. Not only that,

00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:44.480
but he got some cue from these lamas,
who use what we call

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:48.640
as supra-conscious areas,
and just possessed people,

00:17:48.640 --> 00:17:50.720
that they could not see through.

00:17:50.720 --> 00:17:53.600
And it’s the most dangerous thing
and it is only the

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:57.200
Germans who are enlightened
can oppose it outright.

00:17:57.200 --> 00:18:00.160
It’s absolute nonsense.

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:02.400
Yes,
but that to me was something like Kali,

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:03.840
a Kali experience.

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:04.960
No, no, not at all!

00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:08.000
Kali would kill all of them and she has.
She has killed

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:09.760
and she’ll go on killing all of them.

00:18:09.760 --> 00:18:13.600
But the aim to do it was to…

00:18:13.600 --> 00:18:16.480
They were seekers, wouldn’t you agree?

00:18:16.480 --> 00:18:20.560
No, not at all. No, no. No, by no chance.

00:18:20.560 --> 00:18:25.200
How can seekers be that unkind and… No,
no, no, not by any chance.

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:29.440
Don’t be mistaken. I have seen one
or two of them in Argentina.

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:33.440
Horrible people,
they are very right-sided, fiery,

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:36.720
horrible. You see, they are sinister.

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:39.280
If they were not sinister,
they would not have been possessed

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:42.640
that much, I can tell you that way.
They are not needed

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:44.640
because what good are they going to do?

00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:46.000
What right have they got?

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:49.680
Because they have got straight noses,
that’s why they think they can do…

00:18:49.680 --> 00:18:52.080
What good can they do to the world?
Nothing!

00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:57.360
They cannot do any good to the world,
nothing. A spiritual person cannot

00:18:57.360 --> 00:18:59.600
side with them at all, in no way.

00:18:59.600 --> 00:19:02.800
If a spiritual person is like this,
they are the other way round, anti-God.

00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:06.560
So you think Hitler was a devil, in a way?

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:10.480
Hundred percent, two thousand percent.

00:19:10.480 --> 00:19:13.040
He was a great devil, no doubt about it.

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:17.680
He looked a devil.
It’s God who killed him.

00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:19.440
Do you know how he was tricked?

00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:23.280
Perhaps you do not know how he
was tricked by Kali herself, you see.

00:19:23.280 --> 00:19:25.680
The trick was like this.

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:29.200
First he learned from these lamas
that a swastika, if it is used,

00:19:29.200 --> 00:19:32.160
he’ll be saved to do whatever he wants,
because swastika is the sign of innocence.

00:19:32.160 --> 00:19:35.920
Yes,
it’s a kind of mala that would keep him.

00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:41.040
Yes, that’s what. So he gave him,
they took the protection under swastika

00:19:41.040 --> 00:19:45.040
and they used the stencil,
stencil to paint it.

00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:49.840
Stencil is something which we cut out
and then you put colour through that.

00:19:49.840 --> 00:19:54.160
What do you call a stencil? Like a plate.

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:04.080
So he was using stencils.
Lots of stencils were

00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:09.120
used for painting tanks, painting this,
painting that, all were used stencils.

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:12.640
But what happened,
the stencils got exhausted and so they had

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:14.960
to use the same stencils
the other way round.

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:18.240
When he started using the other way round,
it was the other swastika

00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:20.400
which was for destruction.

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:25.040
Ah yes, it moved backwards, the wheel,
the swastika.

00:20:25.040 --> 00:20:28.320
That’s how he got destroyed.
It’s God’s trick.

00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:34.720
He was the greatest devil
I could ever think of. Horrible,

00:20:34.720 --> 00:20:41.360
worst possible man you
could ever think of. No doubt.

00:20:41.360 --> 00:20:46.800
Do you think there is something in common
between the Indian people and the Germans?

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:51.360
Because the Aryas,
they of course are in India,

00:20:51.360 --> 00:20:52.800
were in India as well.

00:20:53.840 --> 00:21:00.560
I don’t find anything like that, because,
I mean, a Hitler can never be in India.

00:21:00.560 --> 00:21:06.240
He cannot. He’ll have to die. I mean,
we won’t allow Hitler to come up in India.

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:09.920
He cannot work out in India. Gandhi can.

00:21:09.920 --> 00:21:12.160
It’s the other side, yes.

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:17.440
In our philosophy or in our life, you see,
we are very forgiving people,

00:21:17.440 --> 00:21:24.720
extremely forgiving. And we never attack,
India never attacked any country so far,

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:26.320
never.
Not even Pakistan.

00:21:26.320 --> 00:21:29.200
That was just once
because Pakistanis were a bit too much,

00:21:29.200 --> 00:21:31.600
only once. Once they attacked.

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:36.000
That’s only an exception to prove the rule
because they were a bit too much.

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:39.760
They were not attacking,
but they were having people killed,

00:21:39.760 --> 00:21:41.200
you see, here and there and there.

00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:46.240
So we had to open a war. Otherwise,
there was no way out for us.

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:48.400
That was the only once they did it.

00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:52.320
But otherwise, it’s such a big history
of thousands of years,

00:21:52.320 --> 00:21:56.000
we never attacked any country
when so many attacked us.

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:58.720
Three hundred years we lived in slavery.

00:22:00.240 --> 00:22:01.979
So you think there is a difference,
a big difference.

00:22:01.979 --> 00:22:04.000
Yes, very different. Very,
very different type of people.

00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:06.480
Absolutely very different.
We are extremely forgiving.

00:22:06.480 --> 00:22:09.600
We are very hospitable.
We are very kind people.

00:22:09.600 --> 00:22:12.720
If you come to Indian villages,
they have been asked them,

00:22:12.720 --> 00:22:15.840
very hospitable and very innocent.

00:22:15.840 --> 00:22:19.920
And they don’t know how to
kill other human beings.

00:22:19.920 --> 00:22:21.920
It’s out of question.

00:22:21.920 --> 00:22:24.720
Is it a kind of matriarchy?

00:22:24.720 --> 00:22:28.080
Yes. It’s matriarchy.
We are very matriarchal.

00:22:28.080 --> 00:22:30.000
That’s the point is, matriarchy.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:33.440
We believe in the Mother, throughout.
That’s why Shakti.

00:22:33.440 --> 00:22:36.400
And the Kali also killed rakshasas
and devils.

00:22:36.400 --> 00:22:40.560
She did not kill her own children
or she didn’t kill her people

00:22:40.560 --> 00:22:43.200
or in any way her creation.

00:22:43.200 --> 00:22:45.280
One day, she was very annoyed, one day.

00:22:45.280 --> 00:22:49.680
They say she was extremely annoyed
the way the world was going on.

00:22:49.680 --> 00:22:54.942
Annoyed.

00:22:54.942 --> 00:22:54.960
Kali.
Yes. Oh, yes.

00:22:54.960 --> 00:22:59.120
In one of her incarnations,
she was very annoyed. And then she said,

00:22:59.120 --> 00:23:01.520
“No use having this creation anymore.

00:23:01.520 --> 00:23:03.760
Better destroy it, the whole creation”.

00:23:03.760 --> 00:23:06.960
And she started destroying because
there were so many devils and all that.

00:23:06.960 --> 00:23:09.520
She said, “Just destroy this creation”.

00:23:09.520 --> 00:23:12.640
So Shiva thought that,
“How to save the world now?

00:23:12.640 --> 00:23:14.240
It’s impossible”.

00:23:14.240 --> 00:23:18.320
So he put her own child under her feet.

00:23:18.320 --> 00:23:22.320
And she just saw her child under her feet,
and a big tongue came out, “Oh God,

00:23:22.320 --> 00:23:25.280
am I killing my own children?”

00:23:25.280 --> 00:23:27.360
Like Niobe in the Greek saga.

00:23:27.360 --> 00:23:30.160
You must have seen her form like that.

00:23:30.160 --> 00:23:32.320
Yes.
That is the child. Her own child.

00:23:33.120 --> 00:23:36.720
What do you think about abortion?

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:42.480
Abortion,
I would say it’s a modern complication.

00:23:42.480 --> 00:23:47.920
And in… say, for example, for Sahaja Yoga,
we don’t allow abortions to take place

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:50.640
because great souls are
born to Sahaja Yogis.

00:23:50.640 --> 00:23:53.120
So we don’t allow them
to have abortions at all.

00:23:53.120 --> 00:23:55.680
But they have very few children also.

00:23:55.680 --> 00:24:00.160
And now I would say,
the pressure that we have in India,

00:24:00.160 --> 00:24:05.680
maybe because, you see, we would say that,
you see,

00:24:05.680 --> 00:24:11.600
children like to be born in India. See,
here it is minus. In London,

00:24:11.600 --> 00:24:14.960
it is minus because in London,
children are killed.

00:24:14.960 --> 00:24:19.360
Children are killed every week.
Two children are killed.

00:24:19.360 --> 00:24:21.440
You are speaking of abortion
or of tragic accident?

00:24:21.440 --> 00:24:23.200
No, no, just without abortion.

00:24:23.200 --> 00:24:25.680
Just their own children they kill.

00:24:25.680 --> 00:24:29.040
They are killing their own children.

00:24:29.040 --> 00:24:32.640
There are child abuses,
all kinds of horrors. We don’t have…

00:24:32.640 --> 00:24:34.560
we have never known,
we have never even heard

00:24:34.560 --> 00:24:38.240
of these things in India. Any mother even,
she will have ten children

00:24:38.240 --> 00:24:41.200
or twelve children,
she would not kill her child.

00:24:41.200 --> 00:24:44.160
But the modern Indian women, I think…

00:24:44.160 --> 00:24:47.520
They are influenced by you people.
What can we do?

00:24:47.520 --> 00:24:50.880
You see, under the influence of the West,
I would say, they may do.

00:24:50.880 --> 00:24:54.960
But she won’t kill by any chance,
even if she may be westernized or modern.

00:24:54.960 --> 00:24:57.600
No, no, no question of killing.
It is not possible.

00:24:57.600 --> 00:25:00.640
That we can’t think of. You see,
the kindness to the

00:25:00.640 --> 00:25:05.520
children is one of the signs
that shows spirituality

00:25:05.520 --> 00:25:07.920
and fondness of flowers.

00:25:07.920 --> 00:25:11.760
That’s the sign of a spiritual person.

00:25:11.760 --> 00:25:17.960
Why do Indian people like to die,
it seems?

00:25:17.960 --> 00:25:18.320
Die?

00:25:18.320 --> 00:25:21.600
To die.
Because there are so many people in India

00:25:21.600 --> 00:25:24.240
that are dying and they don’t care.

00:25:24.240 --> 00:25:28.320
They don’t seem to care as much as here.
Here, you know,

00:25:28.320 --> 00:25:33.200
you try to find a medical care, the best,
always to avoid death.

00:25:33.200 --> 00:25:35.680
We leave it to God, you see.
We leave it to God.

00:25:35.680 --> 00:25:37.680
That God will look after us.

00:25:37.680 --> 00:25:39.760
And that’s how they live it.

00:25:39.760 --> 00:25:42.000
But here the people are so much worried.

00:25:42.000 --> 00:25:44.720
But cancer is so much here, schizophrenia.

00:25:44.720 --> 00:25:47.920
We don’t have schizo- because you are
so anxious about your life.

00:25:47.920 --> 00:25:50.880
All the time the anxiety,
anxiety eats you off.

00:25:50.880 --> 00:25:54.560
But there we are not anxious,
not least bothered. You see,

00:25:54.560 --> 00:25:58.960
we don’t mind dying also,
because we believe in the second birth.

00:25:58.960 --> 00:26:00.960
That’s one of the greatest faith we have.

00:26:00.960 --> 00:26:04.080
Then doesn’t matter if we die,
we’ll be born again.

00:26:04.080 --> 00:26:07.040
But let us lead a relaxed
life depending on God,

00:26:07.040 --> 00:26:10.160
whatever is his desire.

00:26:10.160 --> 00:26:12.960
But then,
I don’t think the death rate of children

00:26:12.960 --> 00:26:20.160
is much more than of the older people,
because maybe that there are so many

00:26:20.960 --> 00:26:24.960
problems on the hygiene of the children.

00:26:24.960 --> 00:26:27.120
They can’t afford, perhaps, maybe.

00:26:27.120 --> 00:26:34.320
But if you see the proportion which,
what we have, our birth rate, then

00:26:34.320 --> 00:26:37.920
and also proportion to our population,
I would say we are existing

00:26:37.920 --> 00:26:41.440
better than anywhere else, in proportion.

00:26:43.120 --> 00:26:46.640
I mean, if you go on the minor side,
on the population,

00:26:46.640 --> 00:26:49.360
after some time maybe there
may not be left anyone,

00:26:49.360 --> 00:26:50.720
despite all the medication.

00:26:50.720 --> 00:26:54.160
Yes, maybe they want to leave this
world somehow and one day

00:26:54.160 --> 00:26:57.680
Europe doesn’t exist anymore
because there are no people left.

00:26:57.680 --> 00:27:00.960
That’s what they believe in, you see,
that we will…

00:27:00.960 --> 00:27:05.440
they believe that as long as possible,
we should try to live, you see,

00:27:05.440 --> 00:27:12.240
in this world. But it’s not important
one individual life. Supposing,

00:27:12.240 --> 00:27:14.800
I don’t live, my children will live.

00:27:14.800 --> 00:27:19.120
And even if I don’t live, I’ll live again.

00:27:19.120 --> 00:27:24.640
This is the attitude. So doesn’t matter;
not to be anxious. For example,

00:27:24.640 --> 00:27:29.360
from India, only these Westernized people
will go in for a transplant. I mean,

00:27:29.360 --> 00:27:31.760
it’s all right. If there’s a heart attack,
all right, one day I’m going to

00:27:31.760 --> 00:27:35.840
die with heart attack. So what?

00:27:35.840 --> 00:27:47.040
Yes, but it’s difficult
if you fear to leave your body. At least,

00:27:47.040 --> 00:27:48.400
I do. I couldn’t say…

00:27:48.400 --> 00:27:51.600
Because you are conditioned that way,
you see. You are conditioned.

00:27:51.600 --> 00:27:52.706
You have been, yes…

00:27:52.706 --> 00:27:53.280
It’s a deep fear.

00:27:53.280 --> 00:27:54.960
It’s a deep fear. I don’t know.

00:27:54.960 --> 00:27:57.680
We don’t have fear of death at all.
We are not afraid.

00:27:57.680 --> 00:27:59.280
What is death after all?

00:27:59.280 --> 00:28:03.760
It’s just changing your clothes.
So we are not afraid.

00:28:03.760 --> 00:28:06.560
We are not anxious people.
That’s the main thing.

00:28:06.560 --> 00:28:09.280
If you are thinking all the time,
death has to come.

00:28:09.280 --> 00:28:12.160
Whatever is born has to be dead.

00:28:12.160 --> 00:28:14.800
Don’t you think that’s a naivete?

00:28:14.800 --> 00:28:16.800
No, naivete. It’s the fact.

00:28:16.800 --> 00:28:19.760
That’s a fact. Yes,
but you can say that’s a fact…

00:28:19.760 --> 00:28:24.880
You see, intellectualism is sometimes mad,
I tell you.

00:28:24.880 --> 00:28:27.520
Because they don’t see the fact, you see.

00:28:27.520 --> 00:28:33.200
If you start thinking about it,
one has to die, in any case.

00:28:33.840 --> 00:28:39.120
Whatever is born has to die. So,
there’s no naivete in this thought.

00:28:39.120 --> 00:28:41.120
It’s a fact. It’s a factual thing.

00:28:41.120 --> 00:28:44.640
If you accept something factual,
then it is naive.

00:28:44.640 --> 00:28:50.320
But I think it is better to
be naive than to be imaginary.

00:28:50.320 --> 00:28:52.160
In the false sense.

00:28:52.160 --> 00:28:55.840
I mean, everyone has to die, no doubt.
I mean,

00:28:55.840 --> 00:29:01.200
is there anybody who has survived so far?

00:29:01.200 --> 00:29:07.920
Yes, but finally I want,
or everybody might want to stop

00:29:07.920 --> 00:29:10.720
being rebirthed again and again.

00:29:10.720 --> 00:29:12.627
Eternal life. For that,
you must take your to spiritually.

00:29:12.627 --> 00:29:13.120
Finally, one death…

00:29:13.120 --> 00:29:16.960
That should be so. But
if you are interested in your bodily life,

00:29:16.960 --> 00:29:18.800
then it has to die, because body.

00:29:18.800 --> 00:29:22.800
But your Spirit doesn’t die. That’s true.

00:29:22.800 --> 00:29:25.440
For eternal life,
you have to come to your Spirit.

00:29:26.640 --> 00:29:30.960
That’s very true. But if you are coming
there for your body’s sake,

00:29:30.960 --> 00:29:35.360
then you won’t get to it. If you are
so much worried about your body,

00:29:35.360 --> 00:29:38.640
then you will be strangled by your body.

00:29:38.640 --> 00:29:43.040
But if you don’t care for your body,
it’s all right. Now that’s a sign of

00:29:43.040 --> 00:29:44.160
a spiritual life also.

00:29:44.160 --> 00:29:49.520
So now I would say that I have lived
always in comfort in my father’s house,

00:29:49.520 --> 00:29:51.280
in my husband’s house, of course.

00:29:51.280 --> 00:29:54.800
I have all the comforts of life,
everything. But if you ask Me,

00:29:54.800 --> 00:29:59.120
I’ll sleep there on the street,
I have no problem. I can sleep anywhere.

00:29:59.120 --> 00:30:03.360
I can go to the jungles,
I can take bath in the river,

00:30:03.360 --> 00:30:06.320
live there nicely.
I won’t have any problem at all.

00:30:06.320 --> 00:30:09.840
Can you earn your own living?

00:30:09.840 --> 00:30:13.520
I need not. Because, you see,
my husband earns such a lot

00:30:13.520 --> 00:30:16.640
that it’s shameful to earn any more,
I tell you. To be very frank,

00:30:16.640 --> 00:30:19.760
he earns all the money,
he doesn’t pay any tax, nothing.

00:30:19.760 --> 00:30:22.240
So it is a bit too much
of money we have got.

00:30:22.240 --> 00:30:26.160
So it’s not proper for Me to earn.
Why should I earn?

00:30:26.160 --> 00:30:27.840
I just don’t understand.

00:30:27.840 --> 00:30:35.440
Yes, but I feel that, as a woman, I also,
from my childhood, I wanted to be,

00:30:35.440 --> 00:30:37.520
in a way, I wanted to become independent.

00:30:37.520 --> 00:30:39.440
Because the society is such here, no?

00:30:39.440 --> 00:30:43.760
No, but also maybe that was my aim,
the aim of my soul.

00:30:43.760 --> 00:30:45.437
That’s why I was born here in Germany.

00:30:45.437 --> 00:30:48.160
No,
the soul is not bothered about earnings.

00:30:48.160 --> 00:30:54.480
Soul is never bothered. It is only the,
you see, outside it’s a very

00:30:54.480 --> 00:30:56.960
money-oriented country.

00:30:56.960 --> 00:31:01.280
Here money is respected, you see,
every day. Then you start seeing, “Oh,

00:31:01.280 --> 00:31:05.760
I must also have money. Otherwise,
I won’t be respected “. That’s what it is.

00:31:05.760 --> 00:31:07.920
Yes,
but I’m not speaking about a lot of money

00:31:07.920 --> 00:31:11.354
or more money to buy maybe two cars
or something.

00:31:11.354 --> 00:31:11.920
To be independent.

00:31:11.920 --> 00:31:13.520
Yes, just to make my living.

00:31:13.520 --> 00:31:16.480
No, we love to be dependent. We love, yes.

00:31:16.480 --> 00:31:19.480
You love to have a husband.

00:31:19.480 --> 00:31:22.320
I am, of course,
and he loves to have a wife.

00:31:22.320 --> 00:31:24.960
My husband loves to have a wife also.

00:31:24.960 --> 00:31:28.480
And we are interdependent, absolutely.

00:31:28.480 --> 00:31:32.440
Because, of course, he earns the money,
it’s all right. But without Me,

00:31:32.440 --> 00:31:35.920
he can’t exist. I look after him.

00:31:35.920 --> 00:31:38.080
I give him the best food, everything.

00:31:38.080 --> 00:31:40.880
So we are interdependent.
My husband doesn’t know

00:31:40.880 --> 00:31:44.720
how to make even coffee,
even to fry an egg.

00:31:44.720 --> 00:31:45.920
He does not even know how to laugh!

00:31:45.920 --> 00:31:48.160
What does he do today? You are not there.

00:31:48.160 --> 00:31:48.720
I beg your pardon?

00:31:48.720 --> 00:31:49.440
You are not there today.

00:31:49.440 --> 00:31:52.880
Now we have servants in the house.
But otherwise,

00:31:52.880 --> 00:31:55.520
he would have to learn in case,
I’m not there. So it’s all right.

00:31:55.520 --> 00:31:57.280
We’ll adjust it, if I’m not there.

00:31:57.280 --> 00:31:58.880
Because he thinks this is a great work.

00:31:58.880 --> 00:32:01.680
He will allow Me to go out,
do whatever I like.

00:32:01.680 --> 00:32:05.680
Because there’s an understanding,
a rapport, a real love. It is,

00:32:05.680 --> 00:32:08.080
you want to be independent
because there’s no love.

00:32:08.080 --> 00:32:10.400
Even my children are dependent on Me.

00:32:10.400 --> 00:32:15.200
Such big, big girls, you know,
she’s 40 years of age, my daughter.

00:32:15.200 --> 00:32:19.200
And she’s entirely dependent
on Me for anything. Still she goes on,

00:32:19.200 --> 00:32:23.200
“Mommy, mommy”.
She comes and sleeps with Me. And so,

00:32:23.200 --> 00:32:24.960
you see, we are all like that.

00:32:24.960 --> 00:32:27.440
We live very well, very happily.

00:32:27.440 --> 00:32:31.510
But your husband, really,
he likes you to do your work.

00:32:31.510 --> 00:32:32.720
Of course.
He doesn’t …

00:32:32.720 --> 00:32:35.520
No, no, no, no, no, no, no. No,
he helps Me a lot.

00:32:35.520 --> 00:32:36.960
He pays a lot of things.

00:32:36.960 --> 00:32:41.520
He paid in the beginning all my traveling,
even for my halls. For my publicity,

00:32:41.520 --> 00:32:44.640
he used to pay. No,
he is different that way. He understands.

00:32:44.640 --> 00:32:48.480
I mean, he’s a reasonable man
and he’s a very intelligent man.

00:32:48.480 --> 00:32:49.280
He sees that.

00:32:49.280 --> 00:32:50.800
He’s spiritual too?

00:32:50.800 --> 00:32:51.600
Yes, he is.

00:33:14.960 --> 00:33:17.920
In the beginning you said
that it’s actually

00:33:17.920 --> 00:33:20.400
the woman who has the power in India.

00:33:20.400 --> 00:33:20.640
Yes.

00:33:20.640 --> 00:33:28.480
But in books, I understood that in India,
the woman has to obey the husband,

00:33:28.480 --> 00:33:34.800
not in a non-self-respected way,
but as a kind of duty.

00:33:35.600 --> 00:33:40.720
No, it is a kind of a, you see,
a proper social arrangement like that.

00:33:40.720 --> 00:33:47.040
It’s a social arrangement. We have to,
you see, a wife obeys the husband because,

00:33:47.040 --> 00:33:52.080
like, you see, you have a Prime minister
and a deputy Prime minister and like that.

00:33:52.080 --> 00:33:56.960
But a deputy Prime minister must
take orders from the Prime minister.

00:33:56.960 --> 00:33:59.200
All right?
But if deputy Prime minister wants to

00:33:59.200 --> 00:34:02.400
always overrule the Prime minister,
then there will be a chaos.

00:34:02.400 --> 00:34:05.360
To keep a proper society, this is so.

00:34:05.360 --> 00:34:07.680
But still, I would say,
my husband would not buy a

00:34:07.680 --> 00:34:10.640
car without showing it to Me.
He wouldn’t buy anything

00:34:10.640 --> 00:34:12.960
without showing it to Me. I mean,
he can’t take any

00:34:12.960 --> 00:34:16.160
decisions otherwise also.
But it’s all right if he says,

00:34:16.160 --> 00:34:20.320
supposing he wants to have, say,
a pink colour for this room. All right,

00:34:20.320 --> 00:34:23.600
I’ll have the pink. Then he said,
“Do you think you like it?”

00:34:23.600 --> 00:34:26.960
“I think it’s all right,
but you could have little different”.

00:34:26.960 --> 00:34:31.520
“Then better try that”. You see,
if there’s love, you try to please another

00:34:31.520 --> 00:34:35.920
person than to please yourself, you see,
if there is love.

00:34:35.920 --> 00:34:38.720
You see,
the combination works out like this,

00:34:38.720 --> 00:34:46.800
that I would try to please him,
you try to please Me. That’s much better.

00:34:46.800 --> 00:34:49.440
Then you like to depend
and you are secure.

00:34:49.440 --> 00:34:50.800
We are much more secure women.

00:34:50.800 --> 00:34:55.840
We don’t get cancer of the breast
and all that as the women get here.

00:34:55.840 --> 00:34:57.280
We are secure people.

00:34:57.280 --> 00:35:01.680
Yes,
but I think one reason could be for that,

00:35:01.680 --> 00:35:07.680
that the value of female
strength is somehow,

00:35:07.680 --> 00:35:10.152
it seems regarded well in India.

00:35:10.152 --> 00:35:10.720
Yes, of course, of course.

00:35:10.720 --> 00:35:12.000
Because here it’s not.

00:35:12.000 --> 00:35:14.000
You see, because we compete with men.

00:35:14.000 --> 00:35:15.760
That’s why. Yes. We should not.

00:35:15.760 --> 00:35:19.120
That’s why we started to compete.
We compete with men.

00:35:19.120 --> 00:35:22.635
We try to put their value as ours
and that makes a neurotic disturb.

00:35:22.635 --> 00:35:27.360
Yes, neurotic for both of them,
both of them. You see, I always say

00:35:27.360 --> 00:35:30.800
that there are two wheels to a chariot.
All right?

00:35:30.800 --> 00:35:34.720
Now the left is on the left side
and right on the right side.

00:35:34.720 --> 00:35:39.600
Now if you try to, they are equal,
no doubt, but not similar.

00:35:40.160 --> 00:35:45.120
This has to look after the left side and
that has to look after the right side.

00:35:45.120 --> 00:35:49.440
So both have to be equal, no doubt,
but they have to balance

00:35:49.440 --> 00:35:50.640
the whole chariot.

00:35:51.280 --> 00:35:55.680
And when you balance the whole chariot,
then there is no problem.

00:35:55.680 --> 00:36:00.000
Supposing one is small,
then it goes round and round.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:03.920
So it has to be equal, sensibly.
It has to be equal.

00:36:03.920 --> 00:36:06.640
And if it is not equal,
then there’s a problem.

00:36:06.640 --> 00:36:10.160
But if you put the left on the right
and right also on the right,

00:36:10.160 --> 00:36:11.600
then what will happen?

00:36:11.600 --> 00:36:12.480
Accident.

00:36:12.480 --> 00:36:17.040
That’s it. That is, you see,
we have to understand we are women

00:36:17.040 --> 00:36:19.200
and we have to be proud of it.

00:36:19.200 --> 00:36:25.040
Yes, but what do you do if you want
to become a more complex person? That is,

00:36:25.040 --> 00:36:30.480
go,
develop yourself above your feminine sex.

00:36:30.480 --> 00:36:33.592
I want to develop into a universal mother.
To become…

00:36:33.592 --> 00:36:36.080
The man in myself,
I have a male side in myself

00:36:36.080 --> 00:36:38.800
like a man has a female side in himself.

00:36:38.800 --> 00:36:40.280
You’re talking about the right
and the left.

00:36:40.280 --> 00:36:42.880
Yes. Then you go to the extreme of women.

00:36:42.880 --> 00:36:46.800
If the extreme of woman is
a universal Mother like Me.

00:36:46.800 --> 00:36:49.280
You go to the extreme of womanhood.

00:36:50.000 --> 00:36:52.800
But whatever, you see,
whatever is your capacity,

00:36:52.800 --> 00:36:57.600
you move with that.
Supposing your capacity is to move

00:36:57.600 --> 00:37:01.280
like a car.
You can’t move like an aeroplane.

00:37:01.280 --> 00:37:03.120
So move like a car at the best.

00:37:03.120 --> 00:37:06.400
You become Rolls Royce, I can say.

00:37:06.400 --> 00:37:11.680
Yes, but still I don’t get why
or how do I develop my male side,

00:37:11.680 --> 00:37:12.640
being a very woman, very much a woman.

00:37:12.640 --> 00:37:13.520
Why do you want to …?

00:37:13.520 --> 00:37:14.480
Very much a woman.

00:37:14.480 --> 00:37:15.520
You should not. Why do you want?

00:37:15.520 --> 00:37:22.560
You’ll become a heterosexual sex,
what you call that, unisex.

00:37:22.560 --> 00:37:23.600
You’ll become unisex.

00:37:23.600 --> 00:37:29.360
No, no. I think a person that is above
the one side or the other side.

00:37:29.360 --> 00:37:32.640
No, no, that, if you try to do that,
then you become…

00:37:32.640 --> 00:37:32.876
You combine the two.

00:37:32.876 --> 00:37:35.680
You cannot combine. You cannot combine.
A woman,

00:37:35.680 --> 00:37:39.520
if she tries to combine with the men,
then she becomes unisex.

00:37:40.240 --> 00:37:42.080
Androgynous would be made.

00:37:42.080 --> 00:37:43.120
Hum?

00:37:44.080 --> 00:37:45.040
Androgynous.

00:37:45.040 --> 00:37:45.920
Yes.

00:37:45.920 --> 00:37:46.560
What is that?

00:37:46.560 --> 00:37:49.440
That is…

00:37:49.440 --> 00:37:56.320
Unisex means a person who will have,
what we call hermaphrodite

00:37:56.320 --> 00:37:58.000
in the medical terminology.

00:37:58.000 --> 00:37:59.197
Yes, it’s hermaphrodite.

00:37:59.197 --> 00:38:05.200
Hermaphrodite. Yes,
they become hermaphrodite. You see,

00:38:05.200 --> 00:38:06.440
neither here nor there.

00:38:06.440 --> 00:38:12.080
Yes, but I’m talking much more of a,
maybe an image of God. God is,

00:38:12.080 --> 00:38:18.080
speaking of God in a more average sense,
is not a sex anymore. It’s a person,

00:38:18.080 --> 00:38:18.880
it’s a human being.

00:38:18.880 --> 00:38:22.560
No, no, no. But you should understand
that God is in Trinity.

00:38:23.120 --> 00:38:27.840
God exists in Trinity. One,
the God Almighty, all right?

00:38:27.840 --> 00:38:30.800
Then his power, the Primordial Mother.

00:38:30.800 --> 00:38:34.080
And then the Son. We have it in Trinity.

00:38:34.080 --> 00:38:37.440
You see, you cannot,
like a rock of Gibraltar, one thing,

00:38:37.440 --> 00:38:42.400
your nose, your eyes, your mouth,
your ears, you have aspects.

00:38:42.400 --> 00:38:46.000
And female aspect should not be
confused with the male aspect,

00:38:46.000 --> 00:38:49.280
not necessary.
It should be completely developed.

00:38:49.280 --> 00:38:54.000
You see, like mine, and now you can say,
I’m quite a good orator myself.

00:38:55.040 --> 00:38:57.040
I’m a woman, no doubt.

00:38:57.040 --> 00:39:00.080
And I have so many male children of mine.

00:39:00.080 --> 00:39:08.160
I’m here and they respect Me,
because I’m a woman.

00:39:08.160 --> 00:39:12.080
But we must develop our extreme.
By mixing up,

00:39:12.080 --> 00:39:17.440
we have become like a hybrid. You see,
we have become like a hybrid. Now say,

00:39:17.440 --> 00:39:20.440
for example, if you take a hybrid animal.

00:39:20.440 --> 00:39:23.760
Let’s say a hen, hybrid.

00:39:23.760 --> 00:39:24.400
A hen?

00:39:25.520 --> 00:39:29.840
A hen or a cock or something hybrid,
you see. They are neither here nor there.

00:39:30.400 --> 00:39:36.240
Like a hybrid hen, if there’s a vulture
coming on her children, she won’t bother.

00:39:36.240 --> 00:39:39.120
She’ll just look at them,
“Let them be killed, finished”.

00:39:39.120 --> 00:39:43.440
But if it’s an Indian hen, you see,
she would start, “Kiki, kiki, kiki”,

00:39:43.440 --> 00:39:46.320
take all the children under her gown,
she’ll protect it.

00:39:46.320 --> 00:39:48.880
Because their function gets spoiled.

00:39:48.880 --> 00:39:55.760
Functionally, if you are a woman,
you can improve on the same,

00:39:55.760 --> 00:39:58.160
like your Mercedes.

00:39:58.160 --> 00:40:01.840
Yes. Oh.

00:40:01.840 --> 00:40:06.320
Improve on the same. But that is
where women in the West have failed.

00:40:06.320 --> 00:40:07.040
That they…

00:40:07.040 --> 00:40:10.160
I think maybe there are many ways.

00:40:10.160 --> 00:40:11.040
Don’t you, wouldn’t you?

00:40:11.040 --> 00:40:12.160
No, no, no.

00:40:12.160 --> 00:40:19.680
Maybe some women just use a different
way to maybe reach the same.

00:40:19.680 --> 00:40:22.960
Like say, I’ll say Madame Curie, you see,
there was Madame Curie.

00:40:22.960 --> 00:40:27.280
She was a woman and a woman out and out,
if you see her. She was a woman,

00:40:27.280 --> 00:40:29.520
very sweet woman she was,
Madame Curie was.

00:40:29.520 --> 00:40:33.040
Madame Montessori was another woman.
She’s just a woman.

00:40:33.040 --> 00:40:36.240
She didn’t become like a man at all,
nothing of man.

00:40:36.240 --> 00:40:39.840
No, not like a man,
but I’m sure Madame Curie has developed

00:40:39.840 --> 00:40:45.990
some sides that you would call male,
in the sense that she would…

00:40:45.990 --> 00:40:46.000
Which one?

00:40:46.000 --> 00:40:51.760
Like she would search for something,
where a woman doesn’t,

00:40:51.760 --> 00:40:58.880
or the female ambition is not to search,
to go forward. You would say.

00:40:58.880 --> 00:41:04.080
No, but to bear. Her power is to bear,
like the Mother Earth, you see.

00:41:04.080 --> 00:41:07.280
She produces everything and she bears it.

00:41:07.280 --> 00:41:09.520
Like bearing power is tremendous.

00:41:09.520 --> 00:41:13.280
And everybody clings to it. Why to search?
For what?

00:41:13.280 --> 00:41:16.320
What is the purpose of searching?

00:41:16.320 --> 00:41:19.200
What do you get out of it, is the point.

00:41:19.200 --> 00:41:20.720
To make an experience.

00:41:20.720 --> 00:41:22.000
What experience? Of searching?

00:41:22.000 --> 00:41:25.840
The experience maybe of disillusion.

00:41:25.840 --> 00:41:31.280
Could be that it’s an illusion
that you want to find something out. But…

00:41:31.280 --> 00:41:32.240
But you see…

00:41:32.240 --> 00:41:35.600
You don’t know unless you
have found the disillusion.

00:41:35.600 --> 00:41:37.200
You know what I’m talking, what I mean?

00:41:37.200 --> 00:41:41.440
Yes, I understand that, but in that,
you can be lost. In that,

00:41:41.440 --> 00:41:44.320
you can be finished.

00:41:44.320 --> 00:41:48.080
On this experimentation business, you see,
it can be very dangerous,

00:41:48.080 --> 00:41:49.840
because you don’t know what you are doing.

00:41:49.840 --> 00:41:54.720
So why not revert back to people
who are acclaimed as something great,

00:41:54.720 --> 00:41:57.120
spiritually, who are higher people.

00:41:57.120 --> 00:42:00.720
What did they do? They went inside,
not outside.

00:42:00.720 --> 00:42:05.120
Yes, but you know this,
the big story of the West is

00:42:05.120 --> 00:42:11.600
that Eve gave the apple to Adam.
And they lost their…

00:42:12.960 --> 00:42:13.360
Innocence.

00:42:13.360 --> 00:42:19.600
Innocence. And they had to somehow,
enter the world of illusion to maybe

00:42:19.600 --> 00:42:21.120
one day go back to paradise again.

00:42:21.120 --> 00:42:23.760
But that was not a very good thing
that they did.

00:42:23.760 --> 00:42:28.480
It made God very difficult to again
bring human beings to normal sense.

00:42:28.480 --> 00:42:31.280
Isn’t it? And now,
going too far with it should

00:42:31.280 --> 00:42:33.520
be stopped at a point. It has come now.

00:42:33.520 --> 00:42:37.440
Now in America, if you go,
you find there funny type of women I saw,

00:42:37.440 --> 00:42:40.480
black also, with big, big muscles,
you know. They neither…

00:42:40.480 --> 00:42:42.000
I didn’t know what sort of a creature…

00:42:42.000 --> 00:42:44.640
I didn’t know how God could
create such creatures.

00:42:44.640 --> 00:42:48.720
They had breasts and also big,
big muscles like wrestlers, you see,

00:42:48.720 --> 00:42:50.960
and funny looking.
What have they achieved? Nothing,

00:42:50.960 --> 00:42:52.640
I don’t think they have achieved much.

00:42:52.640 --> 00:42:55.720
No peace. What you have to achieve is joy
and peace within.

00:42:55.720 --> 00:42:59.760
You must know your determination,
what have you to achieve.

00:42:59.760 --> 00:43:00.880
What do you want to achieve?

00:43:01.440 --> 00:43:03.120
Maybe they feel joy, I don’t know.

00:43:03.120 --> 00:43:04.400
They don’t. You can see that.

00:43:04.400 --> 00:43:09.440
They are neurotic, all of them,
one and all. You can see very clearly.

00:43:09.440 --> 00:43:12.400
They look aged, absolutely neurotic.

00:43:12.400 --> 00:43:16.960
Well, in my eyes they look it too,
but maybe, I don’t know what they think.

00:43:16.960 --> 00:43:22.240
If you see, if you see the results,
then you can see there’s quarrelling,

00:43:22.240 --> 00:43:26.640
fighting. Children are in an orphanage,
the husband in the orphanage,

00:43:26.640 --> 00:43:30.080
the wife in the orphanage.
What is the net result in

00:43:30.080 --> 00:43:35.360
the societies in the West? Tell Me.
Net result.

00:43:35.360 --> 00:43:40.720
The husband is in the lunatic asylum
or in an orphanage, ultimately,

00:43:40.720 --> 00:43:46.000
at the end of life. And the woman is
somewhere in an orphanage, sitting there,

00:43:46.000 --> 00:43:49.200
and the children in some other orphanage.

00:43:49.200 --> 00:43:53.040
But maybe they have to
learn through such tragedy.

00:43:53.040 --> 00:43:56.000
I mean,
I think it’s high time they better learn.

00:43:56.000 --> 00:43:58.240
We learn it from our saints.

00:43:58.240 --> 00:44:01.760
We don’t learn ourselves. You see,
we think we regard our saints

00:44:01.760 --> 00:44:03.920
as very benevolent people.

00:44:03.920 --> 00:44:05.680
They have done so much benevolence work.

00:44:05.680 --> 00:44:06.880
Why will they tell us lies?

00:44:06.880 --> 00:44:11.040
Listen to them. And according to them,
they said that a woman should be

00:44:11.040 --> 00:44:12.640
like this. We tried. It helps.

00:44:12.640 --> 00:44:17.760
Our society is much more peaceful,
much more helpful. And you see,

00:44:17.760 --> 00:44:22.080
materially also, we are not
so much bound by material things in India,

00:44:22.080 --> 00:44:24.880
not so much.
And when it will materially grow also,

00:44:24.880 --> 00:44:28.480
now we are so, if we are evolved properly,
it doesn’t matter.

00:44:28.480 --> 00:44:32.800
Is it that what you call joy? Yesterday,
you talked about the joy of life.

00:44:32.800 --> 00:44:34.232
What did you say? What is joy for you?

00:44:34.232 --> 00:44:37.200
No, no. Joy is something
that you only achieve through your Spirit.

00:44:37.200 --> 00:44:38.960
And it cannot be described. But it is a…

00:44:38.960 --> 00:44:40.160
So it’s not materialistic?

00:44:40.160 --> 00:44:43.360
No, no, no, nothing.
But a material can give you a joy,

00:44:43.360 --> 00:44:47.760
like you see a beautiful picture or
beautiful flowers or something beautiful.

00:44:47.760 --> 00:44:52.000
The joy starts pouring down,
actually like shivers upon you,

00:44:52.000 --> 00:44:56.080
such beauty!
There’s no thought in between, no thought,

00:44:56.080 --> 00:45:02.960
nothing. I said, I see you,
just I see you. And just you as a creator,

00:45:02.960 --> 00:45:06.400
what the creator has put into you,
just gives me joy. First time,

00:45:06.400 --> 00:45:10.000
you enjoy human beings,
after you are a Spirit. Anything

00:45:10.000 --> 00:45:14.240
that is beautiful doesn’t give you lust,
greed, or any thought in the mind.

00:45:14.240 --> 00:45:21.920
But just the joy of the creation in that
person just comes pouring down into you.

00:45:21.920 --> 00:45:24.240
Can you see my aura?

00:45:24.240 --> 00:45:25.520
No, I don’t want to see it.

00:45:25.520 --> 00:45:27.040
Oh yes, but you could.

00:45:27.040 --> 00:45:28.560
I mean, it’s not necessary.

00:45:28.560 --> 00:45:29.360
Oh yes.

00:45:29.360 --> 00:45:32.880
When you see the aura,
you are on the right side, you see.

00:45:32.880 --> 00:45:34.880
From the right side you see the aura.

00:45:34.880 --> 00:45:36.160
So better not see that.

00:45:36.160 --> 00:45:40.240
What I have to see is your center,
how to do it. And that’s the best way

00:45:40.240 --> 00:45:43.120
to achieve your ascent.

00:45:43.120 --> 00:45:49.280
Because if I want to see your right side,
what’s the use? I don’t want you to

00:45:49.280 --> 00:45:50.400
move on the right side.

00:45:50.400 --> 00:45:52.160
I don’t want you to move on the left.

00:45:52.160 --> 00:45:54.560
I want you to move this way.

00:45:54.560 --> 00:46:00.480
So no use going to the right
or to the left. Seeing aura is of no use.

00:46:00.480 --> 00:46:03.920
I thought
that one sees it maybe all the time,

00:46:03.920 --> 00:46:08.800
and that it shows a certain
state of mind of the moment, or….

00:46:08.800 --> 00:46:14.080
Yes, but why not see the essence of it,
the chakras?

00:46:14.080 --> 00:46:15.920
Chakras are the best to be seen.

00:46:15.920 --> 00:46:19.400
If you can feel the chakras,
you know how to cure it, you’re done.

00:46:19.400 --> 00:46:22.880
It’s as simple as that.
But what is the worst part

00:46:22.880 --> 00:46:25.280
of Western life is that,
that they don’t take

00:46:25.280 --> 00:46:27.760
to Sahaja Yoga easily.
They take to all kinds of

00:46:27.760 --> 00:46:30.800
nonsensical experiences.
They go to these gurus.

00:46:30.800 --> 00:46:35.200
They go to these drugs. I mean,
it’s destructive. All such experiences,

00:46:35.200 --> 00:46:38.160
as I told you yesterday,
that the human awareness,

00:46:38.160 --> 00:46:42.160
when it moves like that,
towards downward movement,

00:46:42.160 --> 00:46:43.440
it is very destructive.

00:46:43.440 --> 00:46:46.880
It destroys you from within and without.

00:46:46.880 --> 00:46:48.960
The whole thing looks
like destruction working.

00:46:48.960 --> 00:46:51.600
Yes,
but the Germans are very much Western.

00:46:51.600 --> 00:46:55.120
So in the beginning you said,
you think the Germans have a

00:46:55.120 --> 00:46:57.120
certain capacity for spirituality.

00:46:57.120 --> 00:46:58.784
You see, only capacity is there.

00:46:58.784 --> 00:46:59.360
Isn’t there a contradiction?

00:46:59.360 --> 00:47:02.960
Non, no, not contradiction,
because it’s a powerful thing.

00:47:02.960 --> 00:47:05.680
It’s a powerful thing.
But if you want to use, say,

00:47:05.680 --> 00:47:08.800
atomic energy, which is a powerful thing,
for constructive work

00:47:08.800 --> 00:47:13.600
you are very powerful,
or destructive also you are very powerful.

00:47:13.600 --> 00:47:17.600
Just now you have to just
turn your faces to that. You are powerful.

00:47:17.600 --> 00:47:20.616
So you think the Kundalini,
the power is very strong in the Germans,

00:47:20.616 --> 00:47:21.436
Strong in you, I mean…
But it’s not a way…

00:47:21.436 --> 00:47:23.840
No, no, no. Your machinery is very good.

00:47:23.840 --> 00:47:26.800
Your machinery is good.
The power has to start.

00:47:26.800 --> 00:47:29.840
If the power starts working,
your machinery will work all right.

00:47:29.840 --> 00:47:32.080
But if you want to go downward,
you will go fast.

00:47:32.080 --> 00:47:35.360
If you want to go upward,
you can go very fast.

00:47:35.360 --> 00:47:37.680
It depends on your attitude.

00:47:37.680 --> 00:47:40.240
And that is where you have failed.

00:47:40.240 --> 00:47:42.960
The attitude is towards going downward.

00:47:42.960 --> 00:47:45.840
That’s what I’m saying,
that it is difficult.

00:47:45.840 --> 00:47:50.720
Also this is a little change,
that you have to change your attitude.

00:47:50.720 --> 00:47:53.520
You have to ascend.
Forget about these things,

00:47:53.520 --> 00:47:57.360
these intellectual things,
this all nonsense, arguments, this, that.

00:47:57.360 --> 00:47:58.960
Forget it. Just get there.

00:47:58.960 --> 00:48:00.240
Forget the head.

00:48:00.240 --> 00:48:02.800
You will. You will, no doubt,
because the Kundalini

00:48:02.800 --> 00:48:05.360
will just pierce through.
You’ll have no thoughts.

00:48:05.360 --> 00:48:10.320
No thoughts at all. Then what will you do?

00:48:10.320 --> 00:48:14.800
I know that, from experience,
that it’s a great relief

00:48:14.800 --> 00:48:16.200
to forget about thoughts.

00:48:16.200 --> 00:48:17.680
Oh, absolutely! You don’t know.

00:48:17.680 --> 00:48:21.600
In Switzerland, one doctor came, he said,
“You cut my throat or do what you like,

00:48:21.600 --> 00:48:23.520
